module singleCellTrapDetection
module antibodyBindingDetection

manifest HybridomaCells
manifest TargetCells
manifest IMDM_Medium
manifest PBS
manifest PluronicF127
manifest HFE7500_Surfactant
manifest AlexaFluor647_SecondaryAb
manifest CellTrace_CFSE
manifest CalceinAM_RedOrange

// ============================================================
// An Automated Single-Cell Droplet-Digital Microfluidic
// Platform for Monoclonal Antibody Discovery.
// Ahmadi, Tran, Letourneau, Little, Fortin, Moraitis, Shih
// Small 2024, 20, 2308950
// DOI: 10.1002/smll.202308950
//
// Platform: Droplet-Digital (D2) microfluidics -- a three-layer
// hybrid device combining a digital microfluidic (DMF) electrode
// layer (Cr on glass, 7 um SU-8 dielectric), and three stacked
// PDMS-based microchannel devices:
//   Device 1 -- Trapping array (100 traps, 50 per side, 20 um
//               channel height, 50-75 um width, 7 um constriction;
//               each trap has 2 actuation electrodes + 1 ground).
//   Device 2 -- Flow-focusing droplet generator (target cells,
//               ~30 pL droplets, ~3 kHz throughput, Poisson
//               encapsulation).
//   Device 3 -- Co-planar binary electrode sorter (selects
//               single-target-cell droplets by CellTrace CFSE
//               fluorescence at 470 nm ex / 520 nm em).
//
// CELL LINES (provided by NRC Canada):
//   Hybridoma cells -- cultured in IMDM + 10% heat-inactivated
//     FBS + mouse IL-6 (1 ng/mL) + pen/strep; 37 C / 5% CO2;
//     passaged every 3 days at 8e6 cells/mL; loaded at 1e6/mL.
//   Target cells -- express membrane-bound antigen; cultured in
//     DMEM + 10% FBS + G418 (0.4 mg/mL); loaded at 1e6/mL.
//
// WORKFLOW SUMMARY (8 steps, Figure 2):
//   A. Target cells encapsulated in ~30 pL droplets (Device 2).
//   B. Single target-cell droplets sorted (Device 3).
//   C. Hybridoma cells loaded and trapped (Device 1).
//   D. In situ droplet generation around trapped hybridomas
//      (phase change: oil at 1 nL/s, electrodes at 32 Vrms /
//      15 kHz; droplet size 40-150 pL).
//   E. Target-cell droplets re-injected and merged with
//      hybridoma droplets in traps (32 Vrms / 15 kHz; highest
//      co-encapsulation efficiency: 95 +/- 3.2% at 5 nL/s).
//   F. Co-incubation on-chip for 30 min at room temperature.
//      Hybridoma secretes mAbs; antigen-specific mAbs bind
//      to target cell membrane-bound antigen.
//   G. Droplet disruption + PBS/Alexa Fluor 647 wash
//      (64 Vrms / 15 kHz; 96.8% fluorescence reduction in
//      one wash step; flow rate 1-5 nL/s).
//   H. Fluorescence detection: antigen-specific mAb droplets
//      are Alexa Fluor 647 positive (lex=627 nm, lem=665 nm).
//      Positive droplets collected by reverse-flow oil release
//      (4 nL/s) into a glass capillary filled with HFE7500.
//
// PERFORMANCE METRICS:
//   Single-cell trapping efficiency: 98 +/- 3.92% at 1 nL/s.
//   Co-encapsulation efficiency:     95 +/- 3.2% at 5 nL/s.
//   Droplet disruption efficiency:   ~100% at 32 Vrms / 1 nL/s.
//   Washing efficiency:              96.8% fluorescence reduction.
//   Cell retention post-wash:        96 +/- 9.6% (1-5 nL/s).
//   Selection rate (100:0 ratio):    94.00 +/- 1.41%.
//   Selection rate (1:50 ratio):     1.60% (rare-cell detection).
//
// NOTE ON DEVICE ABSTRACTION:
//   BioScript `dispense` abstracts reagent loading from
//   gas-tight Hamilton syringes driven by neMESYS pumps.
//   `mix` abstracts both channel-flow hydrodynamic trapping
//   events (Steps C, D) and electrode-actuated droplet
//   merging/washing events (Steps E, G). Duration values
//   reflect the dominant process time at each step.
//   `heat` abstracts the on-chip incubation at ambient
//   temperature (room temperature = 25 C, 30 min).
//   `detect` abstracts fluorescence imaging with the
//   Hamamatsu ORCA-Flash 4.0 camera and photon-counting head
//   (300 ms exposure; lex=627 nm, lem=665 nm for Alexa647).
//   Syringe pump flow-rate values and electrode voltages are
//   annotated in comments; they are not encoded as BioScript
//   primitives (not supported by lilott8/BioScript compiler).
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main                 -- Device priming; target-cell
//                                encapsulation (Device 2);
//                                single-cell sorting (Device 3);
//                                hybridoma trapping (Device 1);
//                                in situ droplet generation;
//                                droplet merge (co-encapsulation);
//                                incubation; wash; detection.
//   BB2  antibodyPass         -- antibodySignal > 0: antigen-
//                                specific mAb detected (Alexa
//                                Fluor 647 positive); collect
//                                droplet and dispose.
//   BB3  antibodyFail         -- antibodySignal <= 0: no specific
//                                mAb; non-binding hybridoma;
//                                drain droplet.
//   BB4  finalCleanup         -- terminal: dispose QC signal;
//                                experiment ends.
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1: Prime Device 1 (trapping array) with 2% Pluronics
//         F-127 in PBS to reduce non-specific cell adhesion
//         to PDMS channel walls.
//         Protocol: flow PBS from inlet 3 at 50 nL/s for 5 min
//         (outlet 1 closed); reduce to 1 nL/s, open outlet 1.
//         NOTE: `mix` here abstracts a channel priming flow,
//         not a DMF electrode mixing step.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

primingPBS      = dispense 1 units of PBS
primingPluronic = dispense 1 units of PluronicF127
primedDevice    = mix primingPBS with primingPluronic for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: Prepare stained target cells for encapsulation.
//         Target cells resuspended in PBS + CellTrace CFSE
//         (5 uM, 1e6 cells/mL); stained 20 min at 37 C,
//         washed with PBS; resuspended in IMDM (10% FBS +
//         IL-6, no antibiotic, 1e6 cells/mL) for Device 2
//         loading.
//         NOTE: `heat` models the 20 min staining incubation.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

targetCells_raw  = dispense 1 units of TargetCells
cfseStain        = dispense 1 units of CellTrace_CFSE
stainedTarget    = mix targetCells_raw with cfseStain for 5s
heat stainedTarget at 37c for 20m

// Wash stained cells with PBS to remove excess dye.
washPBS          = dispense 1 units of PBS
washedTarget     = mix stainedTarget with washPBS for 2s

// Resuspend in IMDM for chip loading.
imdmForTarget    = dispense 1 units of IMDM_Medium
targetCells      = mix washedTarget with imdmForTarget for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3 (Device 2): Encapsulate stained target cells in
//         ~30 pL droplets using flow-focusing droplet
//         generator. Throughput: ~3 kHz; Poisson distribution.
//         Oil: HFE7500 + 2% Ran Fluoro-surfactant.
//         NOTE: `mix` abstracts the flow-focusing encapsulation
//         of target cells in the PDMS microchannel device.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

oilPhase1           = dispense 1 units of HFE7500_Surfactant
targetCellDroplets  = mix targetCells with oilPhase1 for 2s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4 (Device 3): Sort single target-cell droplets using
//         co-planar binary electrode sorter. Fluorescence
//         at 470 nm ex / 520 nm em (CellTrace CFSE) used to
//         distinguish droplets with exactly 1 cell from
//         empty or multi-cell droplets. Sorted droplets
//         collected in a gas-tight glass syringe with HFE oil.
//         NOTE: `detect` abstracts the PMT-based fluorescence
//         counting used to trigger electrode actuation.
//         `singleCellTrapDetection` gates on droplets above
//         the single-cell threshold and below the two-cell
//         threshold (set in the in-house control software).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

sortSignal          = detect singleCellTrapDetection on targetCellDroplets for 10s

// Sort gate: only droplets containing exactly one target cell
// are collected; others are sent to waste.
if (sortSignal > 0) {
    // Single-target-cell droplet selected; hold for re-injection.
    // `targetSortDetection` pass -> droplet transferred to Device 1
    // via 0.014" OD / 0.006" ID tubing bridging Device 2 to Device 3.
    sortedTargetDroplets = mix targetCellDroplets with oilPhase1 for 1s
} else {
    drain targetCellDroplets
}

dispose sortSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5 (Device 1): Prime trapping array with IMDM cell
//         culture media containing hybridoma cells to reduce
//         cell adhesion. Hybridoma cells resuspended in IMDM
//         (10% FBS + IL-6, no antibiotic, 1e6 cells/mL).
//         Stained with CellTrace calcein red-orange AM prior
//         to loading.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

hybridoamCells_raw   = dispense 1 units of HybridomaCells
calceinStain         = dispense 1 units of CalceinAM_RedOrange
stainedHybridoma     = mix hybridoamCells_raw with calceinStain for 5s
heat stainedHybridoma at 37c for 20m

washPBS2             = dispense 1 units of PBS
washedHybridoma      = mix stainedHybridoma with washPBS2 for 2s

imdmForHybridoma     = dispense 1 units of IMDM_Medium
hybridoma_in_imdm    = mix washedHybridoma with imdmForHybridoma for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6 (Device 1 -- Trapping): Load hybridoma cells into
//         the trapping array at 1-5 nL/s. Single cells are
//         hydrodynamically confined in 7 um constriction traps
//         via fluidic resistance (open trap resistance < bypass
//         channel; occupied trap blocks flow to next open trap).
//         Single-cell trapping efficiency: 98 +/- 3.92% at
//         1 nL/s (N=5 repeats, n=10 replicates per flow rate).
//         Device accommodates 100 traps (50 per serpentine side).
//         NOTE: `mix` abstracts the channel-flow hydrodynamic
//         trapping event. Duration (2s) models cell settling
//         at the 7 um constriction.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

trappingMix          = mix primedDevice with hybridoma_in_imdm for 2s

// Verify single-cell occupancy by fluorescence (calcein red-orange:
// lex=577 nm, lem=590 nm). `singleCellTrapDetection` confirms
// single occupancy before proceeding to in situ encapsulation.
trapOccupancySignal  = detect singleCellTrapDetection on trappingMix for 10s

if (trapOccupancySignal > 0) {
    imdmForHybridoma2 = dispense 1 units of IMDM_Medium
    trappedHybridoma = mix trappingMix with imdmForHybridoma2 for 1s
} else {
    drain trappingMix
}

dispose trapOccupancySignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 7 (Device 1 -- In situ droplet generation):
//         Phase change: IMDM cell culture medium replaced by
//         HFE7500 + 2% Ran Fluoro-surfactant oil flowing at
//         1 nL/s through the main channel. Electrodes beneath
//         each trap actuated at 32 Vrms / 15 kHz to shear off
//         aqueous phase and generate in situ droplets
//         (40-150 pL) encapsulating single trapped hybridoma
//         cells. Over 95% of droplets successfully generated
//         at 1 nL/s oil flow rate.
//         NOTE: `mix` abstracts the oil-phase flow + electrode
//         actuation that shears off the aqueous droplet.
//         Duration (4s) models the phase-change dwell time.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

oilPhase2            = dispense 1 units of HFE7500_Surfactant
hybridoamDroplet     = mix trappedHybridoma with oilPhase2 for 4s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 8 (Device 1 -- Co-encapsulation / Merge):
//         Sorted single-target-cell droplets (from Step 4) are
//         re-injected into Device 1 from inlet 2 at 5 nL/s,
//         interleaved with oil spacer from a second inlet at
//         1 nL/s. When a target-cell droplet arrives at a
//         trap, the electrode beneath is actuated (32 Vrms /
//         15 kHz) to merge it with the in situ hybridoma
//         droplet. Co-encapsulation efficiency: 95 +/- 3.2%
//         at 5 nL/s re-injection flow rate (highest reported
//         without preliminary sorting of both cell types).
//         NOTE: `mix` abstracts the electrode-actuated droplet
//         merge event. Duration (1s) models the merge dwell time.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

oilSpacer            = dispense 1 units of HFE7500_Surfactant
spacedTargetDroplets = mix sortedTargetDroplets with oilSpacer for 1s
coEncapsulatedDroplet = mix hybridoamDroplet with spacedTargetDroplets for 1s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 9 (On-chip incubation):
//         Merged two-cell droplets incubated on-chip for 30 min
//         at room temperature (25 C). During incubation:
//           - Hybridoma cells secrete monoclonal antibodies
//             into the confined droplet volume.
//           - Antigen-specific mAbs diffuse and bind to
//             membrane-bound antigens on co-encapsulated
//             target cells.
//           - Non-specific mAbs remain free in the droplet.
//         NOTE: `heat at 25c` models on-chip room-temperature
//         incubation. No external heating element used.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat coEncapsulatedDroplet at 25c for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 10 (Droplet disruption + washing):
//         PBS containing Alexa Fluor 647-conjugated goat
//         anti-mouse IgG (H+L) secondary antibody is flowed
//         into Device 1 main channel from inlet 2 at 1-5 nL/s.
//         Electrodes beneath traps actuated at 64 Vrms /
//         15 kHz to disrupt the droplet interface via
//         electrostatic force (field intensity 2-4 x 10^5 V/m).
//         Droplet contents (non-specific secreted mAbs) are
//         washed out through the constriction opening.
//         Hybridoma and target cells (held by antigen-antibody
//         bond) are retained in the trap.
//         Washing efficiency: 96.8% fluorescence reduction
//         after 1 wash step (~5 min total for 50 traps).
//         PBS/Alexa647 flow rate: 1-5 nL/s during wash;
//         reduced to 0.1 nL/s for droplet re-formation.
//         NOTE: `mix` abstracts the phase-exchange wash cycle.
//         `AlexaFluor647_SecondaryAb` manifest encodes the
//         PBS + Alexa Fluor 647 secondary antibody solution
//         (loaded from inlet 2 at the given flow rate).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

alexaFluorWash       = dispense 1 units of AlexaFluor647_SecondaryAb
washPBS3             = dispense 1 units of PBS
pbsAlexaSolution     = mix alexaFluorWash with washPBS3 for 2s

// Droplet disruption and wash: electrode actuation bursts
// the IMDM droplet interface; PBS/Alexa647 flows through
// the trap removing non-specific antibodies.
washedDroplet        = mix coEncapsulatedDroplet with pbsAlexaSolution for 5m

// Re-form oil droplet around the two cells after washing:
// reduce PBS/Alexa647 flow to 0.1 nL/s; increase HFE7500
// Ran-HFE oil flow back to 5 nL/s to generate a new PBS
// droplet encapsulating the two cells in situ.
oilPhase3            = dispense 1 units of HFE7500_Surfactant
reforumDroplet       = mix washedDroplet with oilPhase3 for 1s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 11 (Fluorescence detection):
//         Trapping array imaged with Hamamatsu ORCA-Flash 4.0
//         (lex=627 nm / lem=665 nm, 300 ms exposure) using
//         Alexa Fluor 647 channel. Antigen-specific mAbs that
//         bound to target cell membrane are labelled by the
//         secondary antibody, generating a localised red
//         fluorescent signal around the target cell.
//         Non-specific mAbs were removed by washing and do not
//         generate signal. SNR significantly higher post-wash
//         for antigen-specific (binding) vs. non-specific
//         (non-binding) hybridoma droplets (P < 0.05).
//         The photon-counting head (PMT) is used to trigger
//         on-demand release of positive droplets.
//         `antibodyBindingDetection` module gates on
//         fluorescence signal intensity above background
//         (mean fluorescence of the cell > mean fluorescence
//         of the surrounding droplet).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

antibodySignal       = detect antibodyBindingDetection on reforumDroplet for 10s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: Antibody binding detection gate
// Pass (BB2): antibodySignal > 0 -> Alexa Fluor 647 signal
//             detected at target cell membrane; hybridoma
//             is producing antigen-specific mAb.
//             Droplet released via reverse oil flow (4 nL/s)
//             from outlet 1 into glass capillary (HFE7500)
//             for downstream characterisation/sequencing.
// Fail (BB3): antibodySignal <= 0 -> no specific binding;
//             non-specific mAb producer; droplet drained.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (antibodySignal > 0) {
    // ------------------------------------------------------------
    // Recovery (pass path):
    // Positive droplet released by reverse oil flow (4 nL/s)
    // from outlet 1 (inlet 3 briefly opened to clear channel).
    // Droplet collected into glass capillary filled with HFE7500.
    // FC-40 (1 mL) added to PTFE membrane to disrupt surfactant-
    // stabilised emulsion; aqueous cell droplet absorbed by
    // membrane, then merged with 10-20 uL IMDM complete medium
    // and transferred to a well-plate for downstream expansion
    // and antibody characterisation assays.
    // NOTE: `mix` abstracts the capillary recovery and FC-40
    // wash; `dispose` marks handoff to downstream workflow.
    // ------------------------------------------------------------
    imdmRecovery   = dispense 1 units of IMDM_Medium
    recoveredCells = mix reforumDroplet with imdmRecovery for 1m
    dispose recoveredCells
} else {
    drain reforumDroplet
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose the antibody detection QC signal droplet.
// Experiment ends; recovered cells proceed to off-chip
// antibody characterisation (sequencing, ELISA, etc.).
// ============================================================

dispose antibodySignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
